# Where this daemon is reached, as opposed to what it is wired to.
#
# --host and --port are command line options rather than rig config settings,
# because they describe the box's network rather than its hardware. The unit
# passes 0.0.0.0:8081 and then appends whatever is set here; argparse takes the
# last of a repeated option, so a --port below wins without the unit being
# edited.
#
# A conffile, so an edit survives an upgrade.
#
#STATEMACHINED_EXTRA_ARGS=--port 9000
#
# --no-mdns for a box that should not advertise itself to consoles on the
# network. The API and the web UI are unaffected; a console then needs this
# rig's address by hand.
#STATEMACHINED_EXTRA_ARGS=--no-mdns
